  "term": "spinal stenosis",
  "definition": "Spinal stenosis, in this packet specifically lumbar spinal stenosis, is described as a common degenerative condition of the spine. It is a condition for which surgical decompression may be used, with outcomes assessed through pain, disability, walking ability, recovery time, imaging findings, and surgery-related complications.",
